{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>A perpetual fire.</b> Even on the Sabbath, even in a state of impurity." "<b>It shall not go out.</b> Even during the journeys. It is the honor of Heaven that its hearth not be idle. What do they do for it? They place a copper pot over it — the words of Rabbi Yehudah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "Reading פסכתר as פס-כתר (copper pot); the word is a Talmudic term of uncertain etymology."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:11.481221610Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}